# Repository Context Loading

Context loading is **not optional** — it is the first step before any work in this repository.

All agents and contributors must:
- understand the governance chain
- load required documentation
- respect constraint boundaries
- follow precedence rules

---

# 1. Mandatory Loading Order

## Before ANY Changes

Read these in order:

1. `CONTEXT.md` — mandatory loading order and precedence chain
2. `AGENTS.md` — complete development rules and constraints
3. All mandatory `docs/` from CONTEXT.md:
   - `docs/GOVERNANCE.md`
   - `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
   - `docs/TESTING.md`
   - `docs/COMMENTS.md`
   - `docs/SECURITY.md`
   - `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md`
   - `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`
   - `docs/REVIEW.md`

---

## MUST

- [ ] read `CONTEXT.md` first
- [ ] read `AGENTS.md` second
- [ ] read ALL mandatory docs above, not only those that seem relevant

---

## MUST NOT

- ❌ skip context loading
- ❌ selectively read only "relevant" docs
- ❌ assume familiarity replaces reading
- ❌ begin changes before loading is complete

---

# 2. Source-of-Truth Precedence

When documents conflict, higher-precedence wins:

| Priority | Source |
|----------|--------|
| 1 | `CONTEXT.md` |
| 2 | `docs/GOVERNANCE.md` |
| 3 | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| 4 | Feature-specific documentation |
| 5 | Inline code comments |

---

## Rule

> If two sources disagree, follow the higher-precedence source and flag the conflict.

---

# 3. Non-Negotiable Constraints

These constraints are **absolute** — no exceptions without human approval.

## Type Safety

- [ ] TypeScript strict mode always enabled
- [ ] no `any` in production code without justification
- [ ] named exports preferred; follow existing patterns

## Architecture

- [ ] Nest: controllers → services → TypeORM / AWS / Claude
- [ ] Lambda package isolated under `lambda/`
- [ ] config from environment via Nest config helpers
- [ ] CloudFormation uses `aws-infra-*` ImportValues

## Testing & Quality

- [ ] 80% Jest coverage thresholds
- [ ] co-located Nest `*.spec.ts` / Lambda `*.test.ts`
- [ ] Conventional Commits enforced
- [ ] never hardcode secrets

---

# 4. Quality Gate

## Required Before Pushing

```bash
make preflight
# or rely on: git push  (husky pre-push runs make preflight)
```

This validates:
- root lint / format / test / build
- lambda lint / test / build

---

## MUST NOT

- ❌ commit without passing staged lint/format hooks
- ❌ skip tests or analysis
- ❌ bypass git hooks (`--no-verify`) unless the user explicitly requests it

---

# 5. Conditional Documentation

| Document | When to Read |
|----------|-------------|
| `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md` | new or changed env vars |
| `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` | new modules, Lambda, CloudFormation |
| `docs/TESTING.md` | new tests or coverage changes |
| `docs/SECURITY.md` | secrets, ECDSA, IAM, logging |
| `docs/REVIEW.md` | PR review severity |
| `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` | branch / commit / PR workflow |
| `docs/COMMENTS.md` | adding non-obvious comments |

---

# 6. Anti-Patterns (DO NOT DO)

## MUST NOT

- begin work without reading governance docs
- assume prior context is sufficient for new tasks
- ignore precedence chain when conflicts arise
- treat constraints as optional guidelines
- push without passing quality gates
- invent findings for intentional AWS constraints (e.g. Rekognition resource `*`)

---

# 7. Validation Checklist

Before starting any work:

- [ ] `CONTEXT.md` read
- [ ] `AGENTS.md` read
- [ ] all mandatory docs read
- [ ] precedence chain understood
- [ ] non-negotiable constraints acknowledged
- [ ] quality gates will be run before push
